From 35f72fd3c39c71479a708157bc870582bc900174 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pieroviano <piero.viano@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 03:04:25 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Phase 5: VisualStyleElement catalogue + VisualStyleRenderer

Closes the VisualStyles namespace - the single largest missing block. The
element hierarchy, class names, part/state structure, property enums and renderer
surface are all taken from the net48 reference (nested-type tree extracted with a
new vstree mode in the api-diff tool).

- VisualStyleElement: the full element catalogue (25 categories, 164 parts,
  ~190 nested types) exposed as VisualStyleElement.<Category>.<Part>.<State>
  (for example VisualStyleElement.Button.PushButton.Normal), plus CreateElement
  and the ClassName/Part/State metadata. Class names use the real theme strings
  (BUTTON, COMBOBOX, EDIT, ...); part/state are sequential indices - metadata only,
  since GTK draws the actual theme.
- 32 VisualStyles property enums (BooleanProperty, ColorProperty, IntegerProperty,
  ThemeSizeType, HitTestCode, ...) with values from the reference.
- TextMetrics struct.
- VisualStyleRenderer: parameter tracking (Class/Part/State) plus drawing and
  query methods. There is no Windows theme service on GTK, so Draw* fall back to
  classic rendering (ControlPaint/TextRenderer) and Get* return sensible defaults
  - a documented deviation.

Net48 public types present 635->859 (missing 399->175); VisualStyles missing
types 225->1. Full suite green at 2329 (+3 tests: element class/part/state
metadata, renderer parameter/query defaults, and a smoke draw into a bitmap).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
